Z||000000||b lo 0||07-24-2000||10:21 AM||||I was brainstorming, and this thought popped into my head.  If you've ever seen Lambo and Ferrari racers, the headlights have been converted from flip-up to fixed, set in the same location behind a sheet of Lexan.  I was thinking, I could remove the (troublesome) pop-up headlight mechanism and cover, and replace it with a headlight bucket made of sheet aluminum (or carbon fiber) and use headlights from an old Geo Storm-you know the really short but wide ones-like 4th gen Camaros, then cover the assembly with 1/4"Lexan or Plexi.  This would look really cool, and would save me from having to fix or replace the actuators.  My dad is a professional electronics technician, so wiring won't be a problem.  Anyone's opinions??<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car<p>[This message has been edited by b lo 0 (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
